{
  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "We have only one completed experiment (config_011: rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200; acc=0.520, F1=0.498), so the most critical uncertainty is whether adding the image modality provides any benefit at all. config_003 (multimodal, singleprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, no aggregation, concat) is the cleanest direct comparison to config_011: it holds the RNA encoder (scvi_n200), profile setting (singleprofile), and absence of aggregation constant, introducing only the image encoder and a simple concat fusion. This isolates the effect of the image modality with minimal confounds. If accuracy improves meaningfully, it justifies investing further budget in exploring image encoder choice, aggregation, and fusion in the multimodal space. If it does not, we learn that image adds little and can redirect budget toward RNA encoder and profile-setting variations. Under a tight budget, resolving this fundamental question first maximizes information gained per experiment."
}

